## Community techniques

- **FFX module loader / DINPUT8 proxy** (`dinput8.dll` → `modules\*.dll`) — ffgriever's
  ff10-file-loader concept — https://github.com/ffgriever
  - The DINPUT8 proxy seam is the standard FFX HD modding loading path.
- **DINPUT8 main-thread seam** (`IDirectInputDevice8::GetDeviceState` vtable slot 9) —
  discovered and proven in-house (2026-06-03, FFX Mod Studio) as the race-free main-thread
  bridge; the `CreateRemoteThread` approach it replaces is a well-known unstable pattern.
- **UnX (Untitled Project X)** — Andon M. Coleman — https://github.com/Kaldaien/UnX
  - The repository-root `LICENSE` is MIT. The reviewed `UnX/cheat.cpp`, `UnX/input.h`, and
    `UnX/config.cpp` file headers state GPLv3-or-later; review used commit
    `faae4359bc5f39872536654fda0f4562dd8b7d36` on 2026-08-22.
  - Origin evidence was limited to behavior and address observations, including timing and
    audio-skip behavior at RVAs `0x00420C00` and `0x0030AEC0`. This project does not ship UnX or
    Special K, and no upstream implementation code or text was copied or adapted. Jarvis-HOOK's
    implementation, packed route, lifecycle, UI, diagnostics, and tests are clean-room work.

## Provenance of our own code

- `SinCoreLib` (ATEL bytecode, monster structs, encodings) was extracted from the
  FFX Mod Studio editor codebase (`FFXProjectEditor/FfxLib`) — our own code.
- `ffx_addresses.h` — the RVA ledger — was built from our own IDA Pro reverse engineering;
  each entry documents its evidence doc.
- `NativeMenuShell.h` / `BattlePhotoMode` — header-only references developed in the
  FFX Mod Studio project (Aurora/arena lanes).

